### ──────────────────────────────────────────────
### Notification Service — IntelliJ HTTP Client
### ──────────────────────────────────────────────
### Run these after triggering ride / payment events
### so that RabbitMQ has produced notifications.
### ──────────────────────────────────────────────

### 1. Get all notifications for a rider
### Replace {{riderId}} with an actual user ID that has triggered rides.
GET http://localhost:8085/api/notifications/user/{{riderId}}
Content-Type: application/json

> {%
    client.test("Returns 200", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200");
    });
    if (response.body.length > 0) {
        client.global.set("notificationId", response.body[0].id);
    }
%}

###

### 2. Get unread notifications for a rider
GET http://localhost:8085/api/notifications/user/{{riderId}}/unread
Content-Type: application/json

> {%
    client.test("Returns 200", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200");
    });
%}

###

### 3. Mark a notification as read
PUT http://localhost:8085/api/notifications/{{notificationId}}/read
Content-Type: application/json

> {%
    client.test("Returns 200", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200");
    });
    client.test("isRead is true", function () {
        client.assert(response.body.isRead === true, "Expected isRead=true");
    });
%}

###

### 4. Get all notifications for a driver
GET http://localhost:8085/api/notifications/user/{{driverId}}
Content-Type: application/json

> {%
    client.test("Returns 200", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200");
    });
%}

###

### 5. Error — Mark non-existent notification as read → 404
PUT http://localhost:8085/api/notifications/000000000000000000000000/read
Content-Type: application/json

> {%
    client.test("Returns 404", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 404, "Expected 404");
    });
%}
